<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Selenga River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Selenga is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, about 1,000 kilometres long, which rises in the mountains of northern Mongolia and flows north into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-baikal">Lake Baikal</a>, providing about half of the lake's inflow. Its basin held important pastures and settlements of steppe peoples, including the Merkits along its lower course and later Mongol and Buryat herders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/selenga-river.jpg" alt="Selenga River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angie at German Wikipedia (Original text: Angie) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Selenga2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
